%% Re-render command (from repo root): npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i docs/diagrams/engine-fallback-chain.mmd -o docs/diagrams/engine-fallback-chain.png -c docs/diagrams/mermaid-config.json -b white -s 2
%% Reference: per docs/DECISION_SPEC.md §2 — when Jev has low confidence it outputs directly and flags for review, without entering the text-LLM chain;
%% a successful text-chain output is not flagged for review; the best-effort fallback (degraded) is always flagged for review. See the README caption for the chain order.
%% The branches naturally stretch the width to 4 columns; the tail is merged into a single node to keep the height down, giving roughly a 1:1 overall ratio.
flowchart TB
    A[Email input] --> B{High-precision rules<br/>can decide?}
    B -- Yes --> Z1["engine: rules<br/>direct output"]
    B -- No --> C{Jev available?}
    C -- Available --> J[Jev structured decision]
    C -- Unavailable / failed --> D["Text LLM chain<br/>only tries providers with a configured key"]
    J -- "≥ 0.85 accepted" --> Z2["engine: jev<br/>direct output"]
    J -- "Below 0.85" --> F2["Output result<br/>and flag needs_review"]
    D -- Success --> Z3["engine: llm<br/>direct output"]
    D -- All failed --> E["engine: degraded<br/>best-effort fallback · flag needs_review"]
    F2 --> G["Manual review queue<br/>confirm / correct / defer / undo / bulk"]
    E --> G
    G --> I[("Audit log review_actions<br/>export automatically overlays human conclusions")]
